{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Speak.</b> Always, speech upon the heart serves to remove the sorrow and anxiety that has passed; likewise, \"and he spoke upon their heart\" (Genesis 50:21)." "And the meaning of <b>Jerusalem</b> is the congregation of Israel." "<b>For her term is fulfilled.</b> Her days were completed; likewise, \"all the days of my term I waited\" (Job 14:14); \"Is not a term set for man?\" [ibid. 7:1]. The commentators said it is as it sounds [literally, i.e., military service], but the first [interpretation] is correct." "<b>For she is pardoned.</b> Completed and finished, like \"until your term is completed, like a hired worker's day\" [Job 14:6]; \"then the land will be appeased\" (Leviticus 26:34), in the sense of \"your iniquity is completed\" (Lamentations 4:22)." "<b>Double.</b> For the troubles that every nation received." "<b>For all her sins.</b> On account of all her sins."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:03.337231511Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}